\title{glmseg: Change-Point Detection in Regression Models via the Max-EM Algorithm}
\description{
Detection of an unknown number of change-points in regression models using the max-EM algorithm, which combines a constrained hidden Markov model with a Classification-EM step. Supports Gaussian (homoscedastic and heteroscedastic), logistic, Poisson, and Weibull accelerated failure time (survival) regression, with covariates, Fused-Lasso and Binary Segmentation initializations, and model selection via BIC (with an optional modified penalty to curb over-segmentation). The method is described in Diabate, Nuel and Bouaziz (2025) \doi{10.1016/j.csda.2025.108278}.
